(Decode the two kinds of death a child process can suffer.

 The raw status word comes from `the reaped status` after a reap; these
 two literals are what the kernel would have written for a program that
 exited with code 7, and for one killed by signal 11.)

see process version "0.1" from "./libprocess.lib".

a number called 'a clean exit' is 1792.
Print "exit code: {'exit code of' of 'a clean exit'}".
Print "crashed: {crashed of 'a clean exit'}".
Print "exited normally: {'exited normally' of 'a clean exit'}".

a number called 'a segfault' is 11.
Print "signal: {'signal of' of 'a segfault'}".
Print "crashed: {crashed of 'a segfault'}".
Print "exited normally: {'exited normally' of 'a segfault'}".
